# Machine Learning Based Buyer Segmentation and Investment Profiling for Real Estate Market Intelligence

## Project Overview

This project uses machine learning techniques to segment real-estate buyers into meaningful customer groups. The objective is to understand buyer characteristics and provide useful investment and marketing insights.

## Objectives

- Clean and prepare real-estate buyer data
- Encode categorical features
- Scale numerical features
- Segment buyers using K-Means clustering
- Apply Hierarchical clustering for comparison
- Determine the optimal number of clusters using the Elbow Method and Silhouette Score
- Interpret the buyer segments
- Provide targeted business recommendations

## Methodology

1. Data Cleaning
2. Feature Encoding
3. Feature Scaling
4. K-Means Clustering
5. Elbow Method
6. Silhouette Score
7. Hierarchical Clustering
8. Cluster Interpretation
9. Business Recommendations

## Results

Five buyer segments were identified using K-Means clustering. The highest Silhouette Score among the tested values was obtained at K = 5.

The largest segment contained 315 buyers and represented the Mainstream Indian Investors group. The High-Satisfaction Dubai Investors group had the highest average satisfaction score of 3.80.

